HireTrack – Command History
1. Verify installations
py --version
pip --version
mysql --version


2. Create virtual environments
python -m venv myenv
py -3.14 -m venv .venv


We decided to use myenv and not .venv.
3. Activate virtual environment
.\myenv\Scripts\Activate.ps1


If PowerShell blocks activation:
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned


Alternative activation command:
(Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned) ; (& .\myenv\Scripts\Activate.ps1)


4. Verify Python inside virtual environment
python --version


5. Upgrade pip
python -m pip install --upgrade pip


6. Install required packages
pip install django
pip install djangorestframework
pip install mysqlclient
pip install Pillow


7. Verify installed packages
python -m django --version
pip show djangorestframework
pip show mysqlclient
pip show Pillow


8. Save project dependencies
pip freeze > requirements.txt


9. Create Django project
python -m django startproject config .


10. Check Django project
python manage.py check



Important commands to remember
These are commands you'll repeatedly use during development.
Command	Purpose
.\myenv\Scripts\Activate.ps1	Activate environment
deactivate	Deactivate environment
python manage.py runserver	Start Django server
python manage.py check	Check project configuration
python manage.py makemigrations	Create migration files
python manage.py migrate	Apply migrations
python manage.py createsuperuser	Create admin user
pip freeze > requirements.txt	Save dependencies

